onds to unexpected events adequately (calmness), concentrates very well (cognitive), solves problems extremely well (technical/problem solving), takes responsibility seriously (reliability), maybe good for long flights.\n- Weaknesses: hot temper (crew), know-it-all (attitude), moody? (hot temper). No explicit teamwork.\n\nNow weigh: For long-distance flights, crew communication and teamwork are crucial. A has leadership but unfriendly; B has wrong tone; C has difficulty communicating; D has hot temper. All have some issues. Which is least problematic? Possibly A's leadership may offset unfriendly? B's wrong tone may be more severe. C's communication difficulty is explicit. D's hot temper is severe.\n\nThus A seems best despite unfriendly. Also A has strong safety anticipation and spatial vision, important for navigation. So provisional preference for A.\n\nWe should note uncertainty: lack of explicit info on stress handling for A, and unknown how unfriendly impacts crew. Also unknown about B's possible teamwork strengths not listed. Ask others if they have any positive communication/teamwork attributes for B, C, D.\n\nNow produce public message."}
